WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.955 --> 00:00:03.788
(soft music)

00:00:03.788 --> 00:00:06.212
- Making drawings on land,
on quite a large scale

00:00:06.212 --> 00:00:07.358
is something people have been doing

00:00:07.358 --> 00:00:09.275
for thousands of years.

00:00:21.182 --> 00:00:25.099
I'm Simon Beck and I make
drawings in the snow.

00:00:30.153 --> 00:00:32.736
(wind blowing)

00:00:36.621 --> 00:00:39.010
It started as a bit of fun

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:41.858
but gradually it's taken over my life.

00:00:41.858 --> 00:00:44.316
(panting)

00:00:44.316 --> 00:00:46.587
A ballpark estimate of footsteps,

00:00:46.587 --> 00:00:49.084
about 5,000 steps in an hour.

00:00:49.084 --> 00:00:50.887
(pulsing music)

00:00:50.887 --> 00:00:52.206
A big drawing,

00:00:52.206 --> 00:00:54.268
two hours measuring, eight hours work.

00:00:54.268 --> 00:00:55.457
(snow crunching)

00:00:55.457 --> 00:00:58.267
You're looking at 40,000 steps.

00:00:58.267 --> 00:01:00.934
(chiming music)

00:01:03.632 --> 00:01:05.604
I started doing it as
an easier alternative

00:01:05.604 --> 00:01:09.771
to hiking up the mountain
when I wanted some exercise.

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:15.745
You start with a drawing
on a piece of paper,

00:01:15.745 --> 00:01:18.328
or else a drawing in your mind.

00:01:22.205 --> 00:01:24.616
Just treating it being like
an orienteering touring map.

00:01:24.616 --> 00:01:26.041
You're just going a certain distance

00:01:26.041 --> 00:01:27.583
in a certain direction,

00:01:27.583 --> 00:01:30.916
determining distances by counting paces.

00:01:31.998 --> 00:01:34.484
It's a very physical exercise.

00:01:34.484 --> 00:01:37.191
It's equivalent to a long
day's walk in the hills

00:01:37.191 --> 00:01:40.524
when you make one of these big drawings.

00:01:51.558 --> 00:01:52.962
I'm just about the only
person in the world

00:01:52.962 --> 00:01:54.879
doing anything like it.

